{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786539069,"nonce":"A/zg2PUTqvupYoM8L3GAsWK47gQ=","title":"Six enum-backed array ceilings in `components/schemas` sit above their enum, and no gate walks them","was":"**What is wrong.** `TestEnumFilterCeilingsMatchTheirEnum` (`test/contract/dto_schema_test.go:1066-1106`) holds every enum-backed array to `maxItems == len(enum)`, but it only ever looks at query parameters: its walk is `params := ops[opID].queryParams(d)` (`:1073`), and nothing in the file walks `components/schemas`. Six enum-backed arrays live there, across four property names, and every single one of them declares a `maxItems` above its enum. There is no counter-example — the number of enum-backed body arrays that agree with their enum is zero."}]}